## Third fix: Hidden scene children inside HelpPanel

### Root cause
`HelpPanel.getSceneChildren()` only returned `[this.container]`. Two other GameObjects are created via `scene.add.*` but never parented into the container:

1. **`maskGraphics`** (Graphics) — A white-filled rectangle used as a Geometry Mask for content scrolling. Created via `scene.add.graphics()` at position (0, contentTopY), filled white (0xffffff), then `setVisible(false)`. Invisible in the game view because Phaser's camera skips invisible objects, but `rt.draw()` renders **regardless of visibility**, causing it to appear as an opaque white block on the left side of screenshots.

2. **`inputBlocker`** (Rectangle) — A full-screen transparent rectangle that blocks input while the panel is open. Also a direct scene child not in the exclusion set.

### Fix
Updated `getSceneChildren()` to include `maskGraphics` and `inputBlocker` (with null guards):

```ts
getSceneChildren(): Phaser.GameObjects.GameObject[] {
    const children: Phaser.GameObjects.GameObject[] = [this.container];
    if (this.maskGraphics) children.push(this.maskGraphics);
    if (this.inputBlocker) children.push(this.inputBlocker);
    return children;
}
```

### Verification
- 441/441 gym tests pass
- `tsc --noEmit` clean
- Commit f4cb37e7
